        <type>bool</type>
        <definition> bool bs4.filter.SoupStrainer.matches_tag</definition>
        <argsstring>(self, Tag tag)</argsstring>
        <name>matches_tag</name>
        <qualifiedname>bs4.filter.SoupStrainer.matches_tag</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>self</type>
          <defname>self</defname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classbs4_1_1element_1_1Tag" kindref="compound">Tag</ref></type>
          <declname>tag</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>Do the rules of this `SoupStrainer` trigger a match against the
given `Tag`?

If the `SoupStrainer` has any `TagNameMatchRule`, at least one
must match the `Tag` or its `Tag.name`.

If there are any `AttributeValueMatchRule` for a given
attribute, at least one of them must match the attribute
value.

If there are any `StringMatchRule`, at least one must match,
but a `SoupStrainer` that *only* contains `StringMatchRule`
cannot match a `Tag`, only a `NavigableString`.
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
